                <pb facs="0568" n="546" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg546"/>

                <head>No. 84.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to General Schenck</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 2,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Confidential. We concur in the opinion that the Arbitrators have the power to
                    adjourn either on their own motion or on the motion of either party.</p>
                <p>If the arguments be put in on both sides on 15th, and Great Britain move for an
                    adjournment, this Government will concur.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
